  "description": "CUJPOQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C212 H250 Cl2 Eu8 N12 O36 S16,x(C3 H7 N1 O1),y(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu01 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu02 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu03 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu04 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu7 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.606-5.123 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.53-179.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu8(μ4-OH)2Cl2(TC4A)4(BCT)2(DMF)5.30(CH3OH)2.70(H2O)2]·3CH3OH·2DMF. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
